## Description

Clicking a session title in the Agents window header renames it inline, but `...` > `Rename...` opened a quick input prompt instead — two different flows for the same operation.

The session header `Rename...` action now renames inline whenever the header can host the input, and only prompts when it cannot (the header is swapped out for the chat tabs row when a created session has a single chat group, or the view is hidden).

### Changes

- **`sessionHeader.ts` / `sessionView.ts`**: `startTitleEditing()` returns `boolean` instead of `void` — `false` when the header is not visible or the session is not renameable — so callers can fall back. A rename already in progress re-focuses/selects its input rather than no-op'ing.
- **`sessionsActions.ts`**: `RenameSessionHeaderAction` tries inline first, then delegates to the existing `sessionsViewPane.renameSession` command for the prompt.
- **`sessionsViewActions.ts`**: the `Menus.SessionBarToolbar` (`...` overflow) entry moves from the quick-pick action to the header action, keeping the same `when`/group/order and `Codicon.edit`. The sessions list context menu keeps the prompt, since that path can target a session that isn't currently mounted.

```ts
override async run(accessor: ServicesAccessor, session: IActiveSession | undefined): Promise<void> {
	if (!session) {
		return;
	}
	if (accessor.get(ISessionsPartService).getSessionView(session.sessionId)?.startTitleEditing()) {
		return;
	}
	await accessor.get(ICommandService).executeCommand(RENAME_SESSION_COMMAND_ID, session);
}
```

### Tests

Cover the new return-value contract on the header, and the action's inline path plus each fallback case (header hidden, no mounted view, no session).

